---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import FormattedDate from '../components/FormattedDate.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const recentPosts = (await getCollection('blog'))
	.sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf())
	.slice(0, 3);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="intro">
				<h1>Anyone can be a product owner now.</h1>
				<p>
					A client called me this spring about something I hadn't been hired for. He'd brought
					me in to help build the thing. Now he wanted to know how to run a pilot, how to do
					early sales, how to craft the narrative for a demo day in front of funders. That's
					not how this started, I thought. But you're asking, so let's go.
				</p>
				<p>
					I keep landing in that spot, and it's always the same shape of organization. It
					understands its impact space better than any consultant ever will. It has real
					funding to build software. And it can go build now, without a hire and without
					waiting for permission. That part is new, and it's good. Then someone says they
					want a site that helps people do a thing, and off it goes. It ships on time,
					exactly to spec, and then it doesn't do what anyone hoped, and there's no good
					word for what went wrong.
				</p>
				<p>
					I want to be in the room when that lands. It's the most useful moment in this
					whole business, and most people go through it by themselves. Engineering makes
					sure a thing gets built right. My job is making sure it's the right thing.
				</p>
				<p class="claim">
					<b>Most funded mission-driven teams never had a product owner. I work as theirs,
					and I leave the team able to do the job without me.</b> Where to invest. In what
					order. How you'll know it worked.
				</p>
				<p class="intro-cta"><a href="/work">The three ways that works &rarr;</a></p>
			</section>

			<section class="recent-posts">
				<h2>Writing</h2>
				<p class="writing-note">
					The tools to build software are catching up to the people who know what's worth building.
					Teachers, caseworkers, organizers, founders: people who have spent years close to real
					problems can now turn what they know into working products. I write about what that
					makes possible, and what it asks of us.
				</p>
				<ul>
					{recentPosts.map((post) => (
						<li>
							<a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`}>
								{post.data.heroImage && (
									<Image width={360} height={240} src={post.data.heroImage} alt="" class="thumb" />
								)}
								<div class="post-text">
									<h3 class="title">{post.data.title}</h3>
									<p class="date">
										<FormattedDate date={post.data.pubDate} />
									</p>
								</div>
							</a>
						</li>
					))}
				</ul>
				<p class="all-posts"><a href="/blog">All posts →</a></p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.intro {
		padding-bottom: 2em;
		margin-bottom: 2em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.intro h1 {
		font-size: 2.25rem;
		line-height: 1.2;
		margin: 0 0 0.75em;
		max-width: 24ch;
	}
	.intro .claim {
		margin-top: 1.5em;
	}
	.intro p {
		max-width: 66ch;
	}
	.intro-cta a {
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--accent);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.intro-cta a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
	.recent-posts h2 {
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
	.writing-note {
		max-width: 66ch;
		margin: 0 0 1.75em;
	}
	.recent-posts ul {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.recent-posts li {
		margin-bottom: 1.5em;
	}
	.recent-posts a {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1.25em;
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.recent-posts .thumb {
		width: 180px;
		height: 120px;
		min-width: 180px;
		object-fit: cover;
		border-radius: 8px;
	}
	.recent-posts a:hover .thumb {
		box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
	}
	.recent-posts .title {
		margin: 0;
		color: rgb(var(--black));
		font-size: 1.25em;
		line-height: 1.3;
	}
	.recent-posts a:hover .title,
	.recent-posts a:hover .date {
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	.recent-posts .date {
		margin: 0.25em 0 0;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}
	.all-posts a {
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--accent);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.all-posts a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.intro h1 {
			font-size: 1.75rem;
		}
		.recent-posts .thumb {
			width: 120px;
			height: 80px;
			min-width: 120px;
		}
	}
</style>
